From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:27:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dxmt: decode BC1/BC3 to RGBA8 on GPUs without BC support,
 plus a format census

A15 reports supportsBCTextureCompression = NO. remap_unsupported_bc() already
created these textures as RGBA8 so the Metal descriptor would validate, but the
upload still carried BC-shaped pitches, so texture_upload_pitch_ok() dropped it
and the texture was never filled. That was Thumper's static and missing art -
the 2026-05-13 workaround's own comment predicted exactly this.

The fix belongs in initWithData because that function derives its entire copy
layout from texture->pixelFormat(), which is still logically BC. Decoding the
data without also switching the layout to the physical format would keep
staging BC-sized rows into an RGBA8 texture.

The logical/physical split stays honest: the D3D resource keeps reporting BC
everywhere - description, pitches, subresources, SRVs are untouched. Only this
upload path uses RGBA8. Surfacing the physical format to the Windows app would
violate D3D semantics even where the game would not notice.

Decode is lossless block expansion, not a re-encode, and runs per subresource
so the largest temporary is one 2048x2048 mip at 16MB, freed immediately. BC1
punch-through (c0 <= c1, index 3 transparent) is handled; BC3's embedded colour
block never uses that mode and is decoded accordingly. Edge blocks decode in
full then clip, as the spec requires for non-multiple-of-4 dimensions. 3D is
excluded - none observed, and guessing at volume slice pitches produces silent
corruption rather than a clean failure.

Scope came from measurement rather than assumption. The census, taken at the
D3D layer before the remap so usage and bind flags still exist, found over real
gameplay: 128 BC resources, 1,234 subresources, BC1 and BC3 only, 30MB total,
all USAGE_DEFAULT with initial data, shader-resource only, zero CPU access,
zero staging, and zero UpdateSubresource/CopyResource/CopySubresourceRegion.
That deleted ASTC, BC7, BC6H, the update path, shadow copies and reverse
conversion from the design.

Verified on device: art correct, zero faults, full mip chains down to 1x1,
peak memory 3007MB against 3013MB before, and 300+ FPS at 640x480 unchanged.

Known census gaps: Map is never hooked, so Map=0 means unmeasured; the copy
probe classifies destinations only, so a BC source copied into a non-BC
destination would be missed.

